      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1324176173,
      "text": "Bidens laevis is a species of flowering plant in the daisy family known by the common names larger bur-marigold and smooth beggarticks. It is native to South America, Mexico, and the southern and eastern United States. It grows in wetlands, including estuaries and riverbanks."
    },
